    "result_text": "All 17 tests pass with a green build. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment rule for `POST /api/owners`. The code is formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` and a 4-digit zero-padded global sequence equal to one more than the current owner count.\n\nChanges, following the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in AGENTS.md:\n\n- **New function step** `AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2014 reads the built `@Val Owner`, computes `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` as the sequence, and sets `customerCode` via `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", last3, sequence)`. It runs before `SaveOwner`, so the count reflects existing owners only (each create sees exactly one more than the previous \u2192 the test's +1 delta holds). Handles short surnames safely with `Math.min(3, len)`.\n- **Wired into** `owners.POST.yml` as a new `assignCode` step between `build` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors.\n- **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter, so it survives to the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read-back. MapStruct maps it to the DTO by name automatically.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a read-only property on the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`/`initials`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n- **Schema files** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the owners table in all four DBs (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). The hsqldb (test DB) has `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be added to `schema.sql`; I also gave the positional `data.sql` owner inserts an explicit column list so the new nullable column doesn't break the seed load.",
